---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../../lib/config';
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Support — videoEx" description="Get help enabling videoEx in Safari, granting website access, using shortcuts, managing settings, and requesting a refund.">
  <Prose title="Support" lead="Help with videoEx on iPhone, iPad, and Mac.">
    <p>Need more help? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <h3>How do I turn on the extension?</h3>
    <p>On Mac, open Safari → Settings → Extensions, check videoEx, and allow it on websites. On iPhone or iPad, open Settings → Apps → Safari → Extensions, turn on videoEx, and allow access under “Allow on Websites.”</p>
    <h3>Why does Safari say videoEx can “read and change web pages”?</h3>
    <p>The extension needs to find video elements on a page to control playback. It only handles video playback; it does not read or save page content, browsing history, or form contents. You can grant or turn off access for each website in Safari settings.</p>
    <h3>Why does videoEx do nothing on a particular website?</h3>
    <p>Refresh the page and check that you have allowed videoEx on that website. Some sites use custom players that videoEx may not be able to control. videoEx works with most web videos in Safari.</p>
    <h3>Why aren't my keyboard shortcuts working?</h3>
    <p>Shortcuts do not trigger while you type in a web page's input field. On Mac, Control + arrow keys can be taken by the system's Mission Control, so the default long-jump shortcuts use Option + arrow keys. You can change shortcuts or restore defaults in the app's Keyboard Shortcuts page.</p>
    <h3>Where do I change settings?</h3>
    <p>Open the videoEx app. The Safari extension popup also has a “Manage Settings in videoEx” link at the bottom.</p>
    <h3>How do I request a refund?</h3>
    <p>Request a refund through Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>
  </Prose>
</BaseLayout>
